post_install() {
  systemd-sysusers audiomuse-ai-worker.conf
  systemd-tmpfiles --create audiomuse-ai-worker.conf

    cat <<'EOF'

AudioMuse-AI worker has been installed.

Review the sample configuration at:

  /etc/audiomuse-ai/worker.env

before starting the service.

Some model artifacts are intentionally not bundled because they are generic
upstream models rather than AudioMuse-specific exports.

CLAP text features require the roberta-base tokenizer to be available
in the Hugging Face cache. Model weights are not required.

This can be downloaded with the Hugging Face CLI:

  hf download roberta-base \
    config.json \
    tokenizer.json \
    tokenizer_config.json \
    vocab.json \
    merges.txt

If the tokenizer is stored in a non-default Hugging Face hub cache, set
HF_HUB_CACHE in:

  /etc/audiomuse-ai/worker.env

Optional features:

  Local lyrics transcription
    Requires a compatible Whisper-small ONNX export.

    The simplest supported setup is:

      audiomuse-ai-whisper-model

    which installs the tested Whisper ONNX export published by AudioMuse-AI.

    Alternatively, another compatible Whisper ONNX export may be used by
    setting LYRICS_WHISPER_MODEL_DIR in:

      /etc/audiomuse-ai/worker.env

  Neural fingerprinting / Search by Recording
    Requires:
      audiomuse-ai-neural-fingerprint

  Gemini AI provider
    Requires:
      python-google-genai

  Mistral AI provider
    Requires:
      python-mistralai

Documentation:
  https://github.com/NeptuneHub/AudioMuse-AI

Start the service with:

  systemctl enable --now audiomuse-ai-worker.service

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  systemd-sysusers audiomuse-ai-worker.conf
  systemd-tmpfiles --create audiomuse-ai-worker.conf
}
